From: Kotesh Murugan <koteshlost@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] psbt: don't assert on attacker-controlled wally errors

Crash signature (Nyx, AFL++, dual_funding scenario, CLN v25.12.1):

    Assertion `wally_err == WALLY_OK' failed.
    bitcoin/psbt.c:268 psbt_add_output()

`psbt_add_tx_output_at()` returns WALLY_EINVAL when the requested insert
index is out of bounds for the underlying tx. The fuzzer reaches this
path through tx_add_output messages whose `serial_id` orders before any
existing output, which can produce an insert_at value libwally rejects.
The assert turns that into a denial-of-service crash on the dualopend
subdaemon.

Returning NULL preserves the existing public contract -- callers that
already handled "PSBT operation failed" branches now see this case too.
The follow-up patches (0003, 0004) wire NULL handling at the two
remaining call-sites that previously assumed success.

---
 bitcoin/psbt.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bitcoin/psbt.c b/bitcoin/psbt.c
--- a/bitcoin/psbt.c
+++ b/bitcoin/psbt.c
@@ -265,8 +265,9 @@ struct wally_psbt_output *psbt_add_output(struct wally_psbt *psbt,

 	tal_wally_start();
 	wally_err = wally_psbt_add_tx_output_at(psbt, insert_at, 0, output);
-	assert(wally_err == WALLY_OK);
 	tal_wally_end(psbt);
+	if (wally_err != WALLY_OK)
+		return NULL;
 	return &psbt->outputs[insert_at];
 }

